diff --git a/doc/developer/StandaloneBuilds.md b/doc/developer/StandaloneBuilds.md
new file mode 100644
index 000000000000..59429142e332
--- /dev/null
+++ b/doc/developer/StandaloneBuilds.md
@@ -0,0 +1,64 @@
+# Standalone Builds of Individual Components
+
+Several Intel-owned components of this repository can be configured and
+built standalone, i.e. against an already-built and installed
+LLVM/DPC++ toolchain (via `find_package(LLVM)` / `-DLLVM_DIR=...`)
+instead of as part of a single monorepo configuration rooted at
+`llvm/`. This is primarily intended for downstream packagers who want
+to build and package components individually.
+
+Standalone mode is detected via `LLVM_MAIN_SRC_DIR`: when the variable
+is unset, the component configures itself standalone. Monorepo builds
+are unaffected by any of the standalone code paths.
+
+Tracking issue: [intel/llvm#21877](https://github.com/intel/llvm/issues/21877).
+
+## General prerequisites
+
+All components need an installed LLVM whose `LLVMConfig.cmake` is
+discoverable, e.g.:
+
+```
+cmake -S <component> -B build \
+  -DLLVM_DIR=<install-prefix>/lib/cmake/llvm \
+  ...
+```
+
+Components that compile device code additionally need the DPC++ tools
+(`clang`, `llvm-spirv`, `sycl-post-link`, ...) from the same install
+available in `LLVM_TOOLS_BINARY_DIR`.
+
+## Per-component configuration
+
+| Component | Source dir | Required cache variables (beyond `LLVM_DIR`) |
+|---|---|---|
+| xptifw | `xptifw/` | `xpti` must be findable as a CMake package (`find_package(xpti)`) |
+| libclc | `libclc/` | none; LLVM tools are resolved from `LLVM_TOOLS_BINARY_DIR` with PATH fallback |
+| libdevice | `libdevice/` | none; optionally `DPCPP_VERSION_MAJOR` (defaults to the in-tree version), `LIBCLC_CUSTOM_LLVM_TOOLS_BINARY_DIR` to override tool lookup. All required tools are validated at configure time. |
+| opencl-aot | `opencl/` | none |
+| spirv-to-ir-wrapper | `llvm/tools/spirv-to-ir-wrapper/` | `LLVM_SPIRV_INCLUDE_DIRS`, `LLVM_SPIRV_LIB` (prebuilt `libLLVMSPIRVLib`) |
+| sycl-jit | `sycl-jit/` | `Clang_DIR`, `LLVM_SPIRV_INCLUDE_DIRS`, `SYCL_JIT_RESOURCE_DIR` (pre-staged resource tree, see below); optional `SYCL_JIT_INCLUDE_TESTS` |
+| sycl | `sycl/` | `Clang_DIR`; OpenCL headers via `find_package(OpenCL)`; when `SYCL_ENABLE_XPTI_TRACING=ON`, prebuilt `xpti`/`xptifw` libraries discoverable via `find_library` |
+
+Component builds that depend on other components (e.g. `sycl` on
+`xptifw`) consume them as installed packages/libraries; build order
+follows the dependency order.
+
+## sycl-jit resources
+
+In the monorepo build, the JIT compiler's embedded resource tree is
+staged by installing the `sycl-headers`, `OpenCL-Headers`,
+`clang-resource-headers` and `libsycldevice` components (plus libclc's
+`libspirv-builtins` when enabled) into a private staging directory. In
+standalone builds this staging pipeline is unavailable; instead, stage
+the same component install trees manually (e.g. with
+`cmake --install ... --component <name> --prefix <dir>` from the
+component builds) and pass the directory as `SYCL_JIT_RESOURCE_DIR`.
+
+## Support expectations
+
+Standalone builds are validated by downstream packaging, not by this
+repository's pre-commit CI. They are supported on a best-effort basis:
+changes must keep monorepo builds byte-identical (which CI does
+enforce), but standalone configurations may occasionally need fixes
+between releases.
